  "question": {
    "text": "A radio active material is reduced to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;of its original amount in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> days. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of the material is left after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> days the initial amount of the material is",
    "image": null
  },
